1
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:29,678
- Colonel Sandurz!
- What is it, Sergeant Ricco?

2
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:35,594
You told me to let you know the moment
Planet Druidia was in sight, sir.

3
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:38,154
- So?
- Planet Druidia's in sight, sir.

4
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:41,036
You're really a Spaceball.

5
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:43,674
- You know that, don't you?
- Thanks, sir.

6
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:47,110
- Have you notified Lord Helmet?
- Yes, sir. He's on his way.

7
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:49,196
Make way for Dark Helmet.

8
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:52,278
All rise in the presence of Dark Helmet.

9
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:41,310
I can't breathe in this thing!

10
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:44,840
- We're approaching Planet Druidia, sir.
- Good.

11
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:48,233
I'll call Spaceball City
and notify President Skroob.

12
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:51,272
I already called him, sir.
He knows everything.

13
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:54,593
What?

14
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:56,995
You went over my helmet?

15
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:59,839
Not exactly over, sir.
Uh, m-m-more to the side.

16
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:03,509
I'll always call you first.
It'll never happen again. Never, ever!

17
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:07,032
Oh, shit!

18
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:09,116
No, no, no, no! No, no!

19
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:12,357
Please, please, please! No, no, not that!

20
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:15,512
Yes, that.

21
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:35,516
- Sandurz!
- Sir?

22
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:37,756
I don't see Planet Druidia. Where is it?

23
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:41,634
We have it on the radar screen.
Shall I punch it up for you?

24
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:44,354
- Nah, I'll do it myself.
- Very good, sir.

25
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:51,635
What's the matter with this thing?
You call that a radar screen?

26
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:54,194
No, sir. We call it... Mr Coffee.

27
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:56,836
Care for some?

28
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,359
Yes!

29
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:01,233
- I always have coffee when I watch radar.
- Of course.

30
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:04,033
- Everybody knows that.
- Of course we do, sir.

31
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:09,196
Now that I have my coffee,
I'm ready to watch radar.

32
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:11,072
Where is it?

33
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:13,998
- Right here, sir.
- Switch to teleview.

34
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:17,310
There it is. Planet Druidia.

35
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:20,432
And under the air shield
10,000 years of fresh air.

36
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:23,395
- We must get through the shield.
- We will, sir.

37
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:28,719
Once we kidnap the princess, her father'll
give us the combination to the air shield,

38
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:32,913
thereby destroying Planet Druidia
and saving Planet Spaceball.

39
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:34,996
Everybody got that?

40
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:38,916
- Good. When will the princess marry?
- Within the hour, sir.

41
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:43,477
Well, I hope it's a long ceremony,
cos it's gonna be a short honeymoon.

42
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:53,917
Hot! Too hot!

43
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:12,397
Oh, if only your mother
were alive to see this day.

44
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:14,476
- Everyone ready?
- Yes, Your Majesty.

45
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:18,275
- No. Where's my droid of honour?
- Oh, dear, yes! Where's Dot?

46
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:19,753
Dot!

47
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:21,836
Dot Matrix!

48
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:23,916
Oh, thank God.

49
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:26,356
- Where have you been?
- Here I am.

50
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:28,471
Sorry. I had to make a pit stop.

51
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:31,194
I'm so excited, I couldn't hold my oil.

52
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:34,073
All right, people. It's magic time.

53
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:36,714
Right, everyone starting on the left foot.

54
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:39,912
- Daddy, that's your right foot.
- It's too late. Keep going.

55
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:54,916
Daddy?

56
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:59,719
- Must I go through with this?
- I'm sorry, my dear. You have to.

57
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:11,076
But, Daddy?

58
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:13,672
I don't love him.

59
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:17,076
I'm sorry, Vespa.
He's the last prince left in the galaxy.

60
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:32,075
Dearly beloved, we are gathered here
on this most joyous occasion

61
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:36,113
to witness Princess Vespa,
daughter of King Roland,

62
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:40,438
going right past the altar,
heading down the ramp, and out the door!

63
00:08:40,760 --> 00:08:43,797
Stop her! Someone, stop her! Stop her!

64
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:47,113
Hey, wait! You forgot to get married.

65
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:48,912
Will you stop?

66
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:52,874
- What are you doing?
- No questions, Dot. Get in!

67
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:05,313
Where is she going?! Where is she going?

68
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:11,391
Come ba...

69
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:12,873
..ck!

70
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:09,796
Barf...

71
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:14,156
Barf.

72
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:17,276
Ba-arf!

73
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:19,469
Huh?

74
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:26,158
- Barf?
- Always when I'm eating.

75
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:33,356
Barf!

76
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:37,156
- What can I do you for?
- Where you been?

77
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:39,555
- Grabbin' a snack. Want some?
- No.

78
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:42,752
- Little hair of the dog?
- No! Listen, answer that for me.

79
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:44,836
- Will you watch that?
- Oh, sorry.

80
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:48,635
I'll just throw on your audio.
That way they won't see you.

81
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:52,150
- Y'hello!
- Hello, Lone Starr.

82
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:53,838
Sorry, wrong switch.

83
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:56,190
Hello, Vinnie. What do you want?

84
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:59,915
No, no, no, no, no, no.
It's not what I want.

85
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:02,873
It's what he wants.

86
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:07,920
Pizza The Hutt!

87
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:10,998
Well, if it isn't Lone Starr

88
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:13,680
and his sidekick, Puke.

89
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:17,954
- That's Barf.
- Barf, Puke, whatever!

90
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:22,633
- Where's my money?
- Don't worry. You'll have it by next week.

91
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:25,228
No, no. I gotta have it by tomorrow.

92
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:28,798
A hundred thousand space bucks...
by tomorrow?!

93
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:30,876
A hundred thousand?

94
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:34,432
No way! You forgot late charges,

95
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:38,394
which brings it up to,
uh... one million space bucks.

96
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:41,751
A million?! That's unfair.

97
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:43,950
Unfair to the pay-or,

98
00:11:44,080 --> 00:11:46,116
but not to the pay-ee.

99
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:50,915
But you're gonna pay it

100
00:11:51,040 --> 00:11:52,598
or else.

101
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:56,876
- Or else what?
- Tell him, Vinnie.

102
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:00,876
Or else Pizza

103
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,594
is gonna send out for you.

104
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:12,078
You're delicious.

105
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:14,156
Ciao, boys.

106
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:39,116
Can we talk?

107
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:42,152
OK, we all know Prince Valium is a pill.

108
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:46,512
But you could've married him for your
father, then had a headache for 25 years.

109
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:51,276
Will you turn that thing off?

110
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:56,152
What?

111
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:58,232
What is it?

112
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:01,511
I was saying,
do you realise what you've done?

113
00:13:01,640 --> 00:13:03,790
Yes! And I'm glad.

114
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:06,878
Glad, glad, glad, glad, glad.

115
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:10,431
I wonder if she's glad.

116
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,956
Don't be ridiculous!

117
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:24,073
As president of Planet Spaceball,
I can assure both you and your viewers

118
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:27,795
that there's absolutely
no air shortage whatsoever.

119
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:31,151
Yes, of course.
I've heard the same rumour myself.

120
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:35,273
Yes, thanks for calling
and not reversing the charges. Yes, bye.

121
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:38,236
Shithead!

122
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:55,430
President Skroob?

123
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:56,709
Yes?

124
00:13:56,840 --> 00:14:00,071
This is Central Control.
Commanderette Zircon speaking, sir.

125
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:01,553
What is it?

126
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:05,116
Lord Helmet has just notified us
that Princess Vespa is in sight.

127
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:08,391
- And Spaceball One is closing in on her.
- Good, good.

128
00:14:08,520 --> 00:14:12,308
We have both ships coming up
on the Teledar, sir, if you wish to observe.

129
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:16,911
- I'll be down immediately.
- Shall I have Snotty beam you down, sir?

130
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:19,793
I don't know about that
beaming stuff. Is it safe?

131
00:14:19,920 --> 00:14:23,390
Oh, yes, sir.
Snotty beamed me twice last night.

132
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:25,829
It was wonderful.

133
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:29,748
All right, I'll take a shot at it.
What the hell, it works on "Star Trek".

134
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,752
Snotty!

135
00:14:35,880 --> 00:14:38,838
- Beam him down.
- Yes, sir. Immediately, sir.

136
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:53,835
Great beasties! His head!

137
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:57,953
- It's on backwards!
- Well, this is terrible! Do something!

138
00:14:58,080 --> 00:15:02,358
I'm sorry, sir. There must have been
a micro-converter malfunction.

139
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:06,393
Why didn't somebody tell me
my ass was so big?

140
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,958
Hold on, sir. We'll try to reverse the beam.

141
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:14,230
Could be the interlocking system.

142
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,195
Lock one. Lock two. Lock three.

143
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:21,673
Loch Lomond.

144
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:34,236
Are you all right, Mr President?

145
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:36,316
Fine, fine, no thanks to you.

146
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:40,319
- We'll beam you back, sir.
- Forget it, forget it. No more beaming.

147
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:42,396
This time I'm gonna walk!

148
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:48,075
President Skroob! Salute!

149
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:50,509
Hail, Skroob!

150
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:55,036
- Hello, President Skroob.
- Oh, uh...

151
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:57,549
- Hello, Charlene.
- I'm Marlene!

152
00:15:57,680 --> 00:16:00,274
- Hello, Marlene.
- I'm Charlene!

153
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:02,436
Chew your gum.

154
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:05,028
- Where's the princess?
- Right there, sir.

155
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:09,676
To the left, approaching Spaceball One
at 1500 light leagues per minute.

156
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:12,360
Good, good! She's almost in our grasp.

157
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:15,438
Tell Dark Helmet
he must take the princess alive.

158
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:24,959
Princess Vespa's spaceship within range.

159
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:29,471
Good.
Fire a warning shot across her nose.

160
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:33,193
What's going on?

161
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:37,074
It's either the Fourth of July,
or someone's trying to kill us!

162
00:16:39,840 --> 00:16:42,752
Hey, I don't have to put up with this.

163
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:44,836
I'm rich.

164
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:48,079
- What are you doing?
- I'm calling my father.

165
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:51,392
1 - 800 - DRUIDIA.

166
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:57,669
Careful, you idiot!
I said across her nose, not up it!

167
00:16:58,240 --> 00:17:00,435
Sorry, sir. Doing my best.

168
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,714
- Who made that man a gunner?
- I did, sir.

169
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:05,558
He's my cousin.

170
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:07,830
- Who is he?
- He's an Asshole, sir.

171
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:12,715
- I know that! What's his name?
- That is his name, sir. Major Asshole.

172
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:16,515
- And his cousin?
- An Asshole, too. Gunner Phillip Asshole.

173
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:19,154
How many Assholes
we got on this ship anyhow?

174
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:21,236
Yo!

175
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:25,749
I knew it. I'm surrounded by Assholes.

176
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:29,715
Keep firing, Assholes!

177
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:33,476
Hurry, Daddy! Hurry!

178
00:17:33,600 --> 00:17:35,795
There are laser blasts all around us!

179
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:37,717
I'm scared.

180
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:43,191
King Roland to Lone Starr!
King Roland to Lone Starr! Are you there?

181
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:48,315
Lone Starr, you've got to help me. My
daughter's being attacked by Spaceballs.

182
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:50,795
Spaceballs? Forget it. Too dangerous.

183
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:54,549
Besides, I'm already numero uno
on Dark Helmet's hit list.

184
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:57,592
Look, Your Highness,
it's not that we're afraid.

185
00:17:57,720 --> 00:18:01,269
It's just that we've got this thing
about death. It's not us.

186
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:04,676
You're the only ones that can save her!
I'll give you anything!

187
00:18:04,800 --> 00:18:06,756
Did you hear me? Anything!

188
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:09,709
- Anything?
- Yes, anything!

189
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:15,312
- OK, we'll do it for... a million.
- A million!

190
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:18,079
Oh, you're starting to fade,
Your Highness.

191
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:20,953
All right, I'll pay it. Only find her, save her.

192
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:23,355
All right, King. You just made a deal.

193
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:25,835
One princess for one million space bucks.

194
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:29,111
- What's she driving?
- A brand-new white Mercedes 2001

195
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:32,630
SEL limited edition.
Moonroof, all-leather interior.

196
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:34,910
I got it at a good price. I paid cash.

197
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:38,237
My cousin Prince Murray has
a dealership. He was very nice to me.

198
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:40,828
We get the idea.
Where was she last seen?

199
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:44,032
- She was just passing Jupiter Two.
- We'll find her.

200
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:46,116
Please, bring her back safely!

201
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:50,396
And if it's at all possible,
try to save the car.

202
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:55,153
One million space bucks!
We can pay off Pizza!

203
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:56,838
Gimme paw!

204
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:05,476
What's happening?

205
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:08,550
What's that glow?

206
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:11,672
- We're not moving.
- Oh, we're moving all right.

207
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:13,756
Backwards!

208
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,116
There's our princess. She's got company.

209
00:19:20,240 --> 00:19:24,119
Oh, no. Spaceballs. And they've
got her in their magnetic beam.

210
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:27,152
Oh, well, we're too late.
I'll just reverse and we'll go.

211
00:19:27,280 --> 00:19:29,589
Barf! No. Bad.

212
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:33,349
Why are we risking our lives
for a princess? I know we need money...

213
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:36,438
Listen!
We're not just doing this for money.

214
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:41,473
We're doing it for a shitload of money!

215
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:44,398
Oh, you're right.
And when you're right, you're right.

216
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:46,078
And you're always right.

217
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:49,954
OK, we save her, but how?
They're gonna spot us on their radar.

218
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:51,035
- Uh-uh.
- Uh-huh.

219
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:52,115
- Uh-uh.
- Uh-huh.

220
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:54,435
Uh-uh, not if we jam it.

221
00:19:54,560 --> 00:19:56,357
Aha! You're right.

222
00:19:56,480 --> 00:19:58,630
- Down scope!
- Down scope.

223
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:07,438
Radar about to be

224
00:20:07,560 --> 00:20:08,913
jammed.

225
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:31,949
Sh...

226
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:33,638
..it!

227
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:40,273
Sir?

228
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:44,234
- What is it?
- Can I talk to you for a moment, sir?

229
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:49,590
- Well?
- Trouble with the radar, sir

230
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:51,950
You don't need that, Private. What is it?

231
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:54,548
Trouble with the radar, sir

232
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:56,750
- What is it?!
- Trouble with the radar.

233
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:59,713
- What's wrong?
- I've lost the bleeps, sweeps and creeps.

234
00:20:59,840 --> 00:21:00,909
- The what?
- The what?

235
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:02,996
You know. The bleeps:

236
00:21:05,520 --> 00:21:07,476
The sweeps:

237
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,956
And the creeps:

238
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:14,076
That's not all he's lost.

239
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:16,839
Sir. The radar, sir. It appears to be

240
00:21:18,560 --> 00:21:20,312
jammed!

241
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:23,116
Jammed.

242
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:28,355
Raspberry.

243
00:21:29,080 --> 00:21:33,631
There is only one man
who would dare give me the raspberry.

244
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:36,636
Lone Starr!

245
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:06,989
- What was that?
- Never mind that. What was that?

246
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:10,313
Hi.

247
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:12,670
- Who are you?
- Barf.

248
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:14,950
Not in here, mister. This is a Mercedes.

249
00:22:15,080 --> 00:22:17,196
No, that's my name. Barf.

250
00:22:17,320 --> 00:22:19,675
Barf? What are you?

251
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:24,635
I'm a mog. Half man, half dog.
I'm my own best friend.

252
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:26,113
What do you want?

253
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:29,710
Your father hired Lone Starr and me
to save you. We gotta go.

254
00:22:29,840 --> 00:22:33,753
- Good. Quick. Hurry. Follow the dog.
- Mog. I'm a mog.

255
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:36,030
Wait. What about my matched luggage?

256
00:22:41,480 --> 00:22:43,675
Hey, stop looking up my can.

257
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:45,552
Sorry.

258
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:55,192
Checking in?

259
00:22:55,320 --> 00:22:57,356
What the hell is all that?

260
00:22:59,240 --> 00:23:01,879
Her Royal Highness's matched luggage!

261
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,558
What?

262
00:23:03,680 --> 00:23:05,955
Her Royal Highness's matched luggage.

263
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:10,831
Oh, matched luggage, huh? What's
she think this is, a Princess Cruise?

264
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:14,990
- Well, she wouldn't go without it.
- Oh, yeah?

265
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:22,154
Now hear this! The minute we get
outta here the first thing we do is

266
00:23:22,280 --> 00:23:24,236
dump the matched luggage!

267
00:23:25,120 --> 00:23:27,076
Who was that?

268
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:30,193
Now you hear this, whoever you are.

269
00:23:30,320 --> 00:23:32,675
You will not touch that luggage

270
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:35,439
And, furthermore,
I want this pigsty cleaned up.

271
00:23:35,560 --> 00:23:38,677
I will not be rescued in such filth.

272
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:42,031
Listen! On this ship,
I don't take orders, I give 'em.

273
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:44,799
This is my dreamboat, sweetheart

274
00:23:44,920 --> 00:23:47,514
- Sweetheart?
- Uh-oh.

275
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:50,630
How dare you speak to me that way!

276
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:53,877
You will address me as
"Your Royal Highness"

277
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:59,632
I am Princess Vespa.
Daughter of Roland, King of the Druids.

278
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:03,756
That's all we needed.

279
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:06,235
A Druish princess.

280
00:24:08,480 --> 00:24:10,835
Funny, she doesn't look Druish.

281
00:24:46,200 --> 00:24:50,159
Now we will show her
who is in charge of this galaxy.

282
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:51,833
Hold it!

283
00:24:51,960 --> 00:24:54,315
I'll handle this personally.

284
00:24:55,400 --> 00:24:57,356
Jawohl, Lord Helmet.

285
00:25:00,360 --> 00:25:02,351
So, Princess Vespa,

286
00:25:02,480 --> 00:25:05,995
you thought you could outwit
the forces of Planet Spaceball.

287
00:25:06,680 --> 00:25:08,671
Well, you were wrong.

288
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:13,351
You are now our prisoner. And you
will be held hostage until such time

289
00:25:13,480 --> 00:25:17,029
as all of the air is transferred
from your planet

290
00:25:17,160 --> 00:25:19,116
to ours.

291
00:25:27,080 --> 00:25:29,230
She's not in there!

292
00:25:30,040 --> 00:25:34,397
Radar repaired, sir. We're
picking up the outline of a Winnebago

293
00:25:34,520 --> 00:25:36,272
Winnebago?

294
00:25:36,400 --> 00:25:38,356
Lone Starr.

295
00:25:39,320 --> 00:25:41,276
Lone Starr...

296
00:25:46,200 --> 00:25:50,671
- Uh-oh, here comes the Badyear blimp.
- We'd better get outta here in a hurry.

297
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:54,236
- Switch to secret hyper jets.
- Switching to secret hyper jets.

298
00:25:54,360 --> 00:25:57,909
Buckle up back there,
we're going into... hyperactive.

299
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:08,310
We're closing in on them, sir.
Soon Lone Starr will be ours.

300
00:26:08,440 --> 00:26:10,954
Good. Prepare to attack.

301
00:26:11,080 --> 00:26:12,433
Prepare to attack!

302
00:26:12,560 --> 00:26:14,869
On the count of three.

303
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:16,592
One

304
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:18,551
two

305
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:21,148
late! What happened? Where are they?

306
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:23,589
I don't know, sir.
They must have hyper jets.

307
00:26:23,720 --> 00:26:26,632
- And what have we got? A Cuisinart?
- No, sir.

308
00:26:26,760 --> 00:26:28,910
- Well, find them! Catch them!
- Yes, sir!

309
00:26:29,040 --> 00:26:32,271
- Prepare ship for light speed.
- No, no, light speed is too slow.

310
00:26:32,400 --> 00:26:35,517
- Light speed too slow?
- Yes. We're gonna have to go right to

311
00:26:35,640 --> 00:26:38,438
- ludicrous speed.
- Ludicrous speed?

312
00:26:38,560 --> 00:26:41,472
We've never gone that fast.
Maybe the ship can't take it.

313
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:44,751
What's the matter, Colonel Sandurz?
Chicken?

314
00:26:46,280 --> 00:26:48,475
Prepare ship...

315
00:26:48,600 --> 00:26:51,273
Prepare ship for ludicrous speed.

316
00:26:51,400 --> 00:26:54,392
Fasten all seat belts.
Seal all entrances and exits.

317
00:26:54,520 --> 00:26:57,956
Close all shops in the mall.
Cancel the three-ring circus.

318
00:26:58,080 --> 00:27:02,551
- Secure all animals in the zoo...
- Shut up, you petty excuse for an officer!

319
00:27:03,400 --> 00:27:06,472
Now hear this. Ludicrous speed!

320
00:27:06,600 --> 00:27:09,353
- Sir, hadn't you better buckle up?
- Oh, buckle this!

321
00:27:09,480 --> 00:27:12,040
Ludicrous speed! Go!

322
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:36,628
What have I done?

323
00:27:37,840 --> 00:27:41,992
My brains... are going into my feet.

324
00:27:52,920 --> 00:27:55,070
What the hell was that?

325
00:27:55,600 --> 00:27:57,556
Spaceball One.

326
00:27:58,240 --> 00:28:00,390
They've gone to plaid!

327
00:28:02,160 --> 00:28:05,516
We passed them! Stop this thing!

328
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:08,514
We can't stop. It's too dangerous.

329
00:28:08,640 --> 00:28:10,676
We've got to slow down first.

330
00:28:11,440 --> 00:28:12,793
Bullshit!

331
00:28:12,920 --> 00:28:16,117
Just stop this thing! I order you!

332
00:28:16,240 --> 00:28:18,959
Stop!

333
00:28:33,320 --> 00:28:35,675
Here, sir, here. Let me help you, sir.

334
00:28:37,640 --> 00:28:40,837
- Are you all right, sir?
- Fine. How have you been?

335
00:28:40,960 --> 00:28:42,518
- Fine, sir.
- Good.

336
00:28:42,640 --> 00:28:44,995
- Good thing you were wearing a helmet.
- Yeah.

337
00:28:45,120 --> 00:28:47,076
What shall we do now, sir?

338
00:28:47,200 --> 00:28:50,112
- Well... Are we stopped?
- We're stopped, sir.

339
00:28:50,240 --> 00:28:52,196
Good.

340
00:28:52,320 --> 00:28:55,790
- Why don't we take a five-minute break?
- Very good, sir.

341
00:28:56,400 --> 00:28:58,356
Smoke if you got 'em.

342
00:29:01,200 --> 00:29:05,034
- Take her out of hyperactive.
- Takin' her out of hyperactive.

343
00:29:07,200 --> 00:29:10,636
Congrats, boss. We did it.
They must've overshot us by a week.

344
00:29:10,760 --> 00:29:14,514
- OK. Set a course for Druidia.
- Setting a course for Drui-i-i-i...

345
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:17,074
- What's that?
- I don't know. We're losin' power.

346
00:29:17,200 --> 00:29:19,156
We're out of gas!

347
00:29:19,280 --> 00:29:22,716
- Must have burned it up in hyper.
- Should've put more than $5 worth in!

348
00:29:22,840 --> 00:29:26,435
OK, we'll have to set her down.
Prepare for an emergency landing.

349
00:29:26,560 --> 00:29:30,075
- Quick, give me a reading.
- "Our Father, who art in heaven..."

350
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:31,758
Stop that!

351
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:34,594
Keep your seat belts on.
You OK, Princess?

352
00:29:36,960 --> 00:29:39,872
No, you idiot!
Where'd you learn how to fly?

353
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:42,230
OK, Eagle Five coming in.

354
00:30:02,720 --> 00:30:05,473
Go left. Right! I mean right! Whoa!

355
00:30:16,800 --> 00:30:20,873
- Where are you going?
- I am going to tell him off once and for all.

356
00:30:21,600 --> 00:30:24,558
W-w-w-wait!
We'll need him to get us out of here.

357
00:30:24,680 --> 00:30:29,151
Called me an idiot? I'm goin' back there
and explain a few things to her.

358
00:30:29,280 --> 00:30:32,829
Besides, he's got a sexy voice.
He might be cute.

359
00:30:33,680 --> 00:30:37,673
- You haven't seen what she looks like.
- I have. All princesses look the same.

360
00:30:37,800 --> 00:30:40,997
Cute! I know these space bums.
They're all alike.

361
00:30:41,120 --> 00:30:43,759
- Fat, ugly,
- Bucktoothed, knock-kneed,

362
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:46,952
- beer-swilling pigs.
- horse-faced space dogs.

363
00:30:47,080 --> 00:30:50,038
Normally I'd...
Ooh! That's gonna leave a mark.

364
00:30:50,640 --> 00:30:52,278
Now, listen, you...

365
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:58,994
You listen. On this ship you're to refer
to me as "idiot", not "you Captain".

366
00:30:59,120 --> 00:31:02,556
- I mean... You know what I mean.
- And you will not call me "you".

367
00:31:02,760 --> 00:31:05,069
You will never address me as "you".

368
00:31:05,200 --> 00:31:07,714
You will call me "Your Royal Highness"!

369
00:31:07,840 --> 00:31:10,195
You are a royal pain in the...

370
00:31:10,320 --> 00:31:12,276
- Whoa! Hold it. Time.
- What?

371
00:31:12,400 --> 00:31:16,393
May I make a suggestion? Any minute
the Spaceballs will make a U-turn,

372
00:31:16,520 --> 00:31:18,715
head back this way and make us all dead.

373
00:31:18,840 --> 00:31:20,592
He's right. Let's go.

374
00:31:20,720 --> 00:31:22,711
Wait. My things.

375
00:31:22,840 --> 00:31:25,308
Now, listen, you royal...

376
00:31:25,440 --> 00:31:26,793
..Highness.

377
00:31:26,920 --> 00:31:30,310
Take only what you need to survive.

378
00:31:49,960 --> 00:31:53,919
Please, slow down.
I'm getting sand up my gears.

379
00:31:56,560 --> 00:31:59,313
Gee, I hope she didn't forget anything.

380
00:32:03,960 --> 00:32:07,953
All right, wait a minute, Barf. Put it down.

381
00:32:08,360 --> 00:32:10,715
- What the hell's in this thing?
- I dunno.

382
00:32:14,720 --> 00:32:18,793
What's this?
I said take only what you need to survive.

383
00:32:19,200 --> 00:32:21,555
It's my industrial-strength hair dryer.

384
00:32:21,680 --> 00:32:23,989
And I can't live without it!

385
00:32:25,200 --> 00:32:29,478
OK, Princess, that's it.
The fairy tale is over.

386
00:32:29,760 --> 00:32:31,910
Welcome to real life.

387
00:32:32,040 --> 00:32:35,794
You want this hot-air machine,
you carry it.

388
00:32:36,080 --> 00:32:37,832
You pick that up.

389
00:32:38,640 --> 00:32:40,676
You pick that up.

390
00:32:40,800 --> 00:32:43,872
How dare you, you insolent peasant!

391
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:46,958
Nobody talks to me that way. Nobody!

392
00:32:47,080 --> 00:32:48,638
Nobody!

393
00:32:48,760 --> 00:32:51,718
Well, what have we got here?
Will you look at her?

394
00:32:52,200 --> 00:32:55,795
Those flashing eyes, those
flushed cheeks, those trembling lips.

395
00:32:55,920 --> 00:32:58,070
You know something, Princess?

396
00:32:58,200 --> 00:33:00,555
You are ugly when you're angry.

397
00:33:00,680 --> 00:33:02,716
- Uh-oh.
- That's it.

398
00:33:02,840 --> 00:33:05,912
- You and your dog are...
- Please, please,

399
00:33:06,040 --> 00:33:08,235
total humans, droids, if I may.

400
00:33:08,360 --> 00:33:11,477
It'll be dark soon,
so I suggest we find a place to camp.

401
00:33:11,600 --> 00:33:13,556
Come, darling.

402
00:33:19,120 --> 00:33:23,352
- See? It's lighter.
- Oh, yeah. This is the best.

403
00:33:24,640 --> 00:33:27,200
I could have carried two or three of these.

404
00:33:29,040 --> 00:33:30,996
Have you found them yet?

405
00:33:31,120 --> 00:33:33,634
No, Lord Helmet.
They're still not on the scanner.

406
00:33:33,760 --> 00:33:35,716
Well, keep looking for them.

407
00:33:44,560 --> 00:33:46,710
Pardon me, sir. I have an idea.

408
00:33:47,000 --> 00:33:50,595
Corporal, get me the video cassette
of "Spaceballs: The Movie".

409
00:33:50,720 --> 00:33:52,676
Yes, sir.

410
00:33:54,960 --> 00:33:58,157
"The Producers", "Blazing Saddles",
"Young Frankenstein"...

411
00:33:58,360 --> 00:34:01,830
- Colonel Sandurz, may I speak with you?
- Yes, sir.

412
00:34:01,960 --> 00:34:05,316
How can there be a cassette
of the movie? We're still making it!

413
00:34:05,440 --> 00:34:08,910
True, sir. But there's been a breakthrough
in home-video marketing.

414
00:34:09,040 --> 00:34:11,554
- There has?
- Yes. Instant cassettes.

415
00:34:11,680 --> 00:34:14,717
They're out in stores
before the movie is finished.

416
00:34:14,840 --> 00:34:16,956
- Nah!
- Here it is, sir.

417
00:34:17,600 --> 00:34:21,036
- "Spaceballs".
- Good work, Corporal. Punch it up.

418
00:34:25,120 --> 00:34:28,078
- Prepare to fast-forward.
- Preparing to fast-forward.

419
00:34:28,200 --> 00:34:30,555
- Fast-forward!
- Fast-forwarding, sir.

420
00:34:48,280 --> 00:34:52,956
No, no, no, go past this. Past this part.
In fact, never play this again.

421
00:34:55,920 --> 00:34:57,876
Try here. Stop.

422
00:35:08,040 --> 00:35:11,191
What the hell am I looking at?
When does this happen in the movie?

423
00:35:11,320 --> 00:35:15,598
Now. You're looking at now. Everything
that happens now is happening now.

424
00:35:15,720 --> 00:35:17,278
- And then?
- We passed then.

425
00:35:17,400 --> 00:35:19,550
- When?
- Just now. We're at now, now.

426
00:35:19,680 --> 00:35:20,874
- Go back to then.
- When?

427
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:21,750
- Now.
- Now?

428
00:35:21,880 --> 00:35:23,279
- Now!
- I can't. We missed it.

429
00:35:23,400 --> 00:35:25,197
- When?
- Just now.

430
00:35:25,320 --> 00:35:28,118
- When will then be now?
- Soon.

431
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:31,912
- How soon?
- Sir, we've identified their location.

432
00:35:32,040 --> 00:35:33,439
- Where?
- The moon of Vega.

433
00:35:33,560 --> 00:35:35,710
- Prepare for our arrival.
- When?

434
00:35:35,840 --> 00:35:38,593
- 1900 hours.
- By tomorrow they'll be our prisoners.

435
00:35:38,720 --> 00:35:40,676
Who?!

436
00:35:57,200 --> 00:36:01,079
- No, thank you. I'm perfectly all right.
- Take it. It's freezing.

437
00:36:01,200 --> 00:36:03,156
If you insist.

438
00:36:10,160 --> 00:36:13,470
- Won't you be cold?
- Nah, cold never bothers me.

439
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:21,433
I can't seem to find Druidia.

440
00:36:21,560 --> 00:36:23,118
It's right there.

441
00:36:23,240 --> 00:36:27,279
- Where?
- There. It's that bright blue one. See?

442
00:36:28,680 --> 00:36:31,433
Oh, yeah, but it's so far a...

443
00:36:32,120 --> 00:36:33,951
..away.

444
00:36:34,160 --> 00:36:36,310
Don't worry. I'll get you there.

445
00:36:37,320 --> 00:36:39,515
- Which one's yours?
- Who knows?

446
00:36:39,640 --> 00:36:43,599
- You don't know where you're from?
- No. I was found outside a monastery.

447
00:36:43,720 --> 00:36:47,474
- Monastery? Where?
- Somewhere in the Ford Galaxy.

448
00:36:48,160 --> 00:36:50,515
Didn't the monks say
who your parents were?

449
00:36:50,640 --> 00:36:53,279
They couldn't. They took a vow of silence.

450
00:36:53,400 --> 00:36:55,960
All I got was this. It was around my neck.

451
00:36:56,080 --> 00:36:57,638
- What is it?
- I don't know.

452
00:36:57,760 --> 00:37:02,311
I've taken it to every wise man in the
universe. Nobody can tell me what it says.

453
00:37:03,520 --> 00:37:05,670
It's beautiful.

454
00:37:06,280 --> 00:37:07,838
You know, I...

455
00:37:10,480 --> 00:37:12,436
It's beautiful.

456
00:37:16,280 --> 00:37:18,919
So, how come you ran away
from your wedding?

457
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:24,073
Well, if you must know,
I wasn't in love with the groom.

458
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:26,953
- Why were you gonna marry him?
- Because!

459
00:37:27,080 --> 00:37:30,231
I'm a princess
and I have to marry a prince.

460
00:37:30,360 --> 00:37:34,148
Ah! And he doesn't do it for you, huh?

461
00:37:34,280 --> 00:37:37,158
No, he doesn't do it for me.

462
00:37:41,080 --> 00:37:43,036
I really must go back.

463
00:37:44,160 --> 00:37:46,469
I shouldn't have run away.

464
00:37:46,840 --> 00:37:52,233
I realise now that love
is one luxury a princess cannot afford.

465
00:37:52,360 --> 00:37:54,396
You're probably right.

466
00:37:54,520 --> 00:37:58,195
I know now that I must learn to live
without... love.

467
00:37:58,320 --> 00:37:59,878
I guess so.

468
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:03,709
- Besides, love isn't that important.
- Nah, it never was.

469
00:38:03,840 --> 00:38:07,116
I could be perfectly happy
the rest of my life without...

470
00:38:08,440 --> 00:38:09,998
..love.

471
00:38:10,120 --> 00:38:12,111
Sure you could.

472
00:38:13,320 --> 00:38:15,515
Without physical contact.

473
00:38:16,400 --> 00:38:17,879
Yeah.

474
00:38:18,040 --> 00:38:20,315
Without being held.

475
00:38:20,440 --> 00:38:22,192
Yeah.

476
00:38:23,080 --> 00:38:25,230
Or kissed.

477
00:38:31,600 --> 00:38:33,556
Abandon ship! Abandon ship!

478
00:38:33,680 --> 00:38:35,830
Women and mogs first!

479
00:38:36,520 --> 00:38:38,590
We'll have none of that, mister.

480
00:38:38,720 --> 00:38:42,030
- How far did he get? What'd he touch?
- Nothing happened.

481
00:38:42,160 --> 00:38:45,232
- What the hell was that noise?
- That was my virgin alarm.

482
00:38:45,360 --> 00:38:48,033
It's programmed to go off before you do.

483
00:38:48,160 --> 00:38:51,311
You get back to bed, miss.
And as for you, sex fiend...

484
00:38:51,440 --> 00:38:55,752
All right, let's all just get some sleep.
We gotta get moving before dawn.

485
00:38:55,880 --> 00:38:58,633
- Why so early?
- Because we're in the middle of a desert,

486
00:38:58,760 --> 00:39:02,958
and we aren't gonna get very far
once that blazing sun gets overhead.

487
00:39:07,160 --> 00:39:09,071
Nice dissolve.

488
00:39:17,920 --> 00:39:19,876
Water. Water.

489
00:39:20,720 --> 00:39:22,472
Water.

490
00:39:30,200 --> 00:39:32,156
Oil. Oil.

491
00:39:33,840 --> 00:39:36,798
Room service. Room service.

492
00:39:41,920 --> 00:39:44,070
Chief, that's it.

493
00:39:46,040 --> 00:39:48,395
I can't... I can't go any further.

494
00:39:50,120 --> 00:39:53,192
- I can't go any further.
- Come on, Barf, old buddy.

495
00:39:53,320 --> 00:39:55,276
- No!
- Just one more dune to go.

496
00:39:55,400 --> 00:39:58,119
No! You said that three dunes ago.

497
00:39:59,040 --> 00:40:00,996
I got no more left.

498
00:40:02,080 --> 00:40:04,275
Oh, waiter. Check, please.

499
00:40:06,960 --> 00:40:08,757
Must go on.

500
00:40:08,880 --> 00:40:10,836
Must go on!

501
00:40:11,640 --> 00:40:13,596
Must go on...

502
00:40:14,560 --> 00:40:16,312
Who am I kidding?

503
00:41:14,320 --> 00:41:16,276
Oh. Thanks, little guy.

504
00:41:17,960 --> 00:41:20,030
Oh, thank you.

505
00:41:22,120 --> 00:41:24,190
Did I miss something?

506
00:41:24,320 --> 00:41:26,470
When did we get to Disneyland?

507
00:41:43,560 --> 00:41:47,792
- I don't see them, Sandurz.
- I've sent the troops on ahead, sir.

508
00:41:47,920 --> 00:41:50,673
- Good. Get moving.
- Driver, prepare to move out.

509
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:53,109
What are you preparing? Just go!

510
00:41:53,240 --> 00:41:54,389
- Just go.
- Yes, sir.

511
00:41:54,520 --> 00:41:56,476
Sir, shouldn't you sit down?

512
00:42:14,520 --> 00:42:18,115
- What are they saying?
- They want us to go with them.

513
00:42:27,560 --> 00:42:31,599
- What is this place?
- It looks like the Temple of Doom.

514
00:42:31,720 --> 00:42:33,790
Well, it ain't Temple Beth Israel.

515
00:42:34,120 --> 00:42:36,918
Come on. I think we better follow 'em.

516
00:42:48,200 --> 00:42:50,350
Oh-oh, I think we woke it up.

517
00:42:51,280 --> 00:42:54,352
- Goodbye. Let me know how it turns out.
- Come back, Dot!

518
00:42:54,480 --> 00:42:57,472
- Come on, we gotta keep goin'.
- We need you.

519
00:43:03,240 --> 00:43:06,630
- What's gonna happen now?
- Don't ask. Maybe it won't.

520
00:43:06,760 --> 00:43:09,911
- What if it does? I'm all for leaving!
- Barf, no!

521
00:43:10,040 --> 00:43:13,112
I think we get outta here now
while the going's good!

522
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:15,752
Silence!

523
00:43:15,880 --> 00:43:21,273
Who dares enter the sacred and awesome
presence of the everlasting know-it-all,

524
00:43:21,400 --> 00:43:23,356
Yogurt?

525
00:43:23,720 --> 00:43:25,472
Yogurt?

526
00:43:34,520 --> 00:43:38,798
- You heard of me?
- Heard of you? Who hasn't heard of you?

527
00:43:38,920 --> 00:43:40,672
Yogurt, the wise.

528
00:43:40,800 --> 00:43:43,837
- Yogurt, the all-powerful!
- Yogurt, the magnificent.

529
00:43:44,280 --> 00:43:48,239
Please, please, don't make a fuss.
I'm just plain Yogurt.

530
00:43:48,360 --> 00:43:50,316
- But you're the one...
- Yes!

531
00:43:50,440 --> 00:43:53,432
I am the keeper of a greater magic.

532
00:43:53,560 --> 00:43:56,074
A power known throughout the universe

533
00:43:56,200 --> 00:43:57,553
- as the...
- Force?

534
00:43:57,680 --> 00:44:00,148
No. The Schwartz.

535
00:44:00,520 --> 00:44:02,476
The Schwartz.

536
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:04,312
Yes.

537
00:44:04,440 --> 00:44:06,192
The Schwartz.

538
00:44:09,440 --> 00:44:13,479
But, Yogurt, what is this place?
What is it that you do here?

539
00:44:13,600 --> 00:44:17,036
- Merchandising.
- Merchandising. What's that?

540
00:44:17,160 --> 00:44:19,435
Merchandising. Come, I'll show you.

541
00:44:19,560 --> 00:44:21,118
Open up the store.

542
00:44:25,920 --> 00:44:28,434
Come! Walk this way! Take a look.

543
00:44:28,560 --> 00:44:31,950
We put the picture's name on everything!

544
00:44:32,080 --> 00:44:34,640
Merchandising! Merchandising!

545
00:44:34,760 --> 00:44:37,320
Where the real money
from the movie is made.

546
00:44:37,440 --> 00:44:40,989
"Spaceballs" - the T-shirt.
"Spaceballs" - the colouring book.

547
00:44:41,120 --> 00:44:45,318
"Spaceballs" - the lunchbox.
"Spaceballs" - the breakfast cereal.

548
00:44:45,440 --> 00:44:47,396
"Spaceballs" - the flame thrower!

549
00:44:48,440 --> 00:44:50,556
The kids love this one.

550
00:44:50,680 --> 00:44:54,070
Last, but not least. "Spaceballs" - the doll.

551
00:44:54,200 --> 00:44:55,997
Me.

552
00:44:56,120 --> 00:44:58,190
May the Schwartz be with you

553
00:45:00,800 --> 00:45:02,552
Adorable.

554
00:45:16,800 --> 00:45:19,075
- President Skroob.
- What is it?

555
00:45:19,200 --> 00:45:22,636
I have an urgent message from
Lord Helmet. He's lost the princess.

556
00:45:22,760 --> 00:45:24,955
- Where?
- Somewhere in the sands of Vega.

557
00:45:25,080 --> 00:45:28,675
Tell them to comb the desert,
do you hear me? Comb the desert!

558
00:45:28,800 --> 00:45:30,756
Yes, sir.

559
00:45:35,600 --> 00:45:37,556
- Sir?
- What?

560
00:45:39,000 --> 00:45:42,356
- Are we being too literal?
- No, you fool, we're following orders

561
00:45:42,480 --> 00:45:45,631
We were told to comb the desert,
so we're combing it

562
00:45:46,040 --> 00:45:48,270
Found anything yet?

563
00:45:48,400 --> 00:45:50,356
Nothing yet, sir.

564
00:45:51,880 --> 00:45:54,155
How about you?

565
00:45:54,280 --> 00:45:56,236
Not a thing, sir.

566
00:45:58,760 --> 00:46:00,751
What about you guys?

567
00:46:00,880 --> 00:46:02,836
We ain't found shit!

568
00:46:05,800 --> 00:46:09,315
It's a big mystery. None of the wise men
could tell me what it means.

569
00:46:09,440 --> 00:46:13,479
Wise men, pshaw. Wise guys, you mean.
What do they know?

570
00:46:13,600 --> 00:46:15,556
Here, let me take a look.

571
00:46:24,240 --> 00:46:27,391
- You can read it!
- No, I was just clearing my throat.

572
00:46:27,520 --> 00:46:29,476
Here, let me take a...

573
00:46:30,200 --> 00:46:32,634
Ah. Ooh, yes.

574
00:46:32,760 --> 00:46:34,990
Yes, yes, of course!

575
00:46:35,120 --> 00:46:36,678
- You understand it?
- Yes.

576
00:46:36,800 --> 00:46:39,360
- What's it say?
- I cannot tell you that now.

577
00:46:39,480 --> 00:46:44,031
- It'll be revealed to you at the proper time.
- Great.

578
00:46:44,160 --> 00:46:47,277
Don't be disappointed.
Back to your Schwartz training.

579
00:46:47,400 --> 00:46:50,836
Here, take the ring.
Point it at that big statue.

580
00:46:50,960 --> 00:46:55,795
OK, but I still don't understand how I'm
gonna lift a big statue with this little ring.

581
00:46:55,920 --> 00:47:00,118
Never underestimate
the power of the Schwartz!

582
00:47:00,240 --> 00:47:02,834
Come on, concentrate. Here we go.

583
00:47:04,240 --> 00:47:05,832
Concentrate.

584
00:47:18,320 --> 00:47:20,880
Lone Starr, you're doing it!

585
00:47:21,000 --> 00:47:22,558
You're doing it!

586
00:47:23,400 --> 00:47:25,709
I can't believe it. The Schwartz is working!

587
00:47:25,840 --> 00:47:27,398
Yes! Yes!

588
00:47:27,520 --> 00:47:29,636
Hey, boss, how'd you do that?

589
00:47:34,120 --> 00:47:36,588
Give me the ring. Give me the ring, quick!

590
00:47:37,480 --> 00:47:41,314
Upsee-dahzee, upsee-mahzee,
upsy-daisy!

591
00:47:47,200 --> 00:47:49,156
Sorry, Barf.

592
00:47:54,080 --> 00:47:56,036
Keep searching.

593
00:47:57,480 --> 00:48:02,429
- It's no use. We've searched everywhere.
- Wait. I feel the presence of

594
00:48:02,560 --> 00:48:03,913
the Schwartz!

595
00:48:04,040 --> 00:48:05,837
- The Schwartz?
- Yes.

596
00:48:05,960 --> 00:48:09,873
It's coming from somewhere... down

597
00:48:10,000 --> 00:48:11,752
there!

598
00:48:13,400 --> 00:48:16,358
You're right, sir.
There's a secret entrance here.

599
00:48:16,480 --> 00:48:19,313
And look at this insignia. It's a "Y".

600
00:48:20,200 --> 00:48:22,475
Yogurt! Yogurt!

601
00:48:22,600 --> 00:48:26,115
I hate yogurt! Even with strawberries.

602
00:48:26,240 --> 00:48:29,038
- I'll call for the attack squad.
- No, we can't go in.

603
00:48:29,160 --> 00:48:31,720
Yogurt has the Schwartz.
It's too powerful.

604
00:48:31,840 --> 00:48:34,308
But, sir, don't you have the Schwartz, too?

605
00:48:34,440 --> 00:48:37,876
He got the upside, I got the downside.
Each Schwartz has two sides.

606
00:48:38,000 --> 00:48:40,639
Then how are we gonna go in there
and get her?

607
00:48:42,040 --> 00:48:44,395
We will not go in there.

608
00:48:44,520 --> 00:48:47,671
She will come out to us.

609
00:48:58,480 --> 00:49:02,234
Vespa, Vespa, my child

610
00:49:02,360 --> 00:49:04,112
Where are you?

611
00:49:04,240 --> 00:49:05,593
Daddy?

612
00:49:05,720 --> 00:49:09,599
Vespa, it's your father, King Roland

613
00:49:09,720 --> 00:49:12,712
- Come to me
- Daddy?

614
00:49:12,840 --> 00:49:15,638
I hear you. I hear you. Where are you?

615
00:49:15,760 --> 00:49:17,716
Follow my voice

616
00:49:18,880 --> 00:49:20,916
Come to me

617
00:49:21,600 --> 00:49:23,556
Come to me

618
00:49:25,800 --> 00:49:27,438
Vespa, where are you going?

619
00:49:27,560 --> 00:49:30,438
Vespa, come to me.

620
00:49:34,320 --> 00:49:37,039
Daddy! Is it really you?

621
00:49:37,160 --> 00:49:40,948
Yes, my dear. I guarantee it.

622
00:49:41,600 --> 00:49:43,556
Would I lie?

623
00:49:45,520 --> 00:49:46,669
Daddy!

624
00:49:47,680 --> 00:49:49,432
No, Vespa, don't!

625
00:49:50,600 --> 00:49:51,953
No.

626
00:49:52,600 --> 00:49:54,556
Fooled you.

627
00:49:57,480 --> 00:50:01,473
Take them both aboard
and put the princess in my quarters.

628
00:50:01,600 --> 00:50:03,556
Now she is mine.

629
00:50:04,160 --> 00:50:07,311
- What are they saying?
- They've taken the princess!

630
00:50:16,400 --> 00:50:18,152
Spaceballs. Too late.

631
00:50:18,480 --> 00:50:20,835
Don't worry, boss. We'll get her back.

632
00:50:21,440 --> 00:50:23,192
Yeah.

633
00:50:24,440 --> 00:50:26,829
- Thanks for the gas, Yogurt.
- You're welcome.

634
00:50:26,960 --> 00:50:30,316
And here. Just in case you get hungry.

635
00:50:31,120 --> 00:50:32,872
- A fortune cookie?
- Yes.

636
00:50:33,000 --> 00:50:36,788
Remember: open it before you eat it.

637
00:50:36,920 --> 00:50:39,150
Thanks. Well, we better get going.

638
00:50:39,280 --> 00:50:41,794
I wonder...
Will we ever see each other again?

639
00:50:41,920 --> 00:50:45,833
Who knows? God willing,
we'll all meet again in "Spaceballs Il:

640
00:50:45,960 --> 00:50:47,916
The Search for More Money".

641
00:50:48,680 --> 00:50:51,433
- Goodbye, Lone Starr.
- Goodbye, Yogurt.

642
00:50:52,720 --> 00:50:54,995
The ring of the Schwartz!

643
00:50:55,120 --> 00:50:58,351
- No, no, I can't take this.
- Take it, take it.

644
00:50:58,640 --> 00:51:01,837
- You might need it.
- Thanks.

645
00:51:01,960 --> 00:51:03,916
I'll never forget you.

646
00:51:04,880 --> 00:51:06,632
Wish me luck.

647
00:51:28,360 --> 00:51:33,559
So, Princess Vespa,
at last I have you in my clutches

648
00:51:33,680 --> 00:51:37,309
to have my way with you
the way I want to.

649
00:51:37,440 --> 00:51:41,319
No! No! Please, leave me alone.
No, you are mine.

650
00:51:41,440 --> 00:51:44,193
Not so fast, Helmet. Lone Starr!

651
00:51:44,320 --> 00:51:47,915
Yes, it's me.
I'm here to save my girlfriend. Hi, honey.

652
00:51:48,040 --> 00:51:50,315
Now you are going to die. Psst!

653
00:51:50,440 --> 00:51:52,590
Oh, oh! Oh!

654
00:51:52,720 --> 00:51:57,191
What'd you do to him? The same thing
I'm going to do to you, big boy. Oh!

655
00:51:57,320 --> 00:51:59,390
And you, too. Oh! Argh!

656
00:51:59,520 --> 00:52:03,308
Now, Princess Vespa, at last we are alone.

657
00:52:03,440 --> 00:52:06,159
Oh, no, I hate you. Leave me alone.

658
00:52:06,280 --> 00:52:10,353
Yet I find you strangely attractive.
Of course you do.

659
00:52:10,480 --> 00:52:14,268
Druish princesses are often
attracted to money and power.

660
00:52:14,400 --> 00:52:17,233
And I have both. And you know it.

661
00:52:17,360 --> 00:52:21,239
Oh, leave me alone. No, kiss me!
No! No! Yes! No!

662
00:52:21,360 --> 00:52:23,316
No! Yes! No! Yes!

663
00:52:26,600 --> 00:52:29,717
Oh, your helmet is so big.

664
00:52:30,240 --> 00:52:31,798
- Lord Helmet.
- What?

665
00:52:31,920 --> 00:52:35,390
- You're needed on the bridge, sir.
- Knock on my door! Knock next time!

666
00:52:35,520 --> 00:52:37,476
- Yes, sir.
- Did you see anything?

667
00:52:37,600 --> 00:52:39,830
No, I didn't see you
playing with your dolls.

668
00:52:39,960 --> 00:52:41,712
Good.

669
00:52:59,120 --> 00:53:00,678
President Skroob.

670
00:53:00,800 --> 00:53:04,395
I told you never to call me on this wall!
This is an unlisted wall.

671
00:53:04,520 --> 00:53:08,433
Sorry, sir, but it's very important.
The princess is in your office

672
00:53:08,560 --> 00:53:10,790
and Lord Helmet is awaiting you there.

673
00:53:10,920 --> 00:53:14,754
- All right, all right. I'll be right there.
- Yes, sir.

674
00:53:25,960 --> 00:53:30,158
Helmet, you fiend! What's going on?
What are you doing to my daughter?

675
00:53:30,280 --> 00:53:33,875
Permit me to introduce
the brilliant young plastic surgeon,

676
00:53:34,000 --> 00:53:35,752
Dr Phillip Schlotkin.

677
00:53:35,880 --> 00:53:40,556
The greatest nose-job man
in the entire universe and Beverly Hills.

678
00:53:40,680 --> 00:53:43,956
- Your Highness.
- Nose job? She's already had a nose job.

679
00:53:44,080 --> 00:53:46,036
It was her Sweet-16 present.

680
00:53:46,160 --> 00:53:49,596
No, it's not what you think.
It's much, much worse.

681
00:53:49,720 --> 00:53:53,156
If you do not give me
the combination to the air shield,

682
00:53:53,280 --> 00:53:56,078
Dr Schlotkin will give your daughter back

683
00:53:56,200 --> 00:53:58,270
her old nose!

684
00:53:58,400 --> 00:54:01,358
No!

685
00:54:02,720 --> 00:54:06,713
- Where did you get that?
- All right, I'll tell. I'll tell.

686
00:54:06,840 --> 00:54:10,310
- No, Daddy, no! You mustn't.
- You're right, my dear.

687
00:54:10,440 --> 00:54:14,558
I'll miss your new nose, but I will not
tell him the combination, no matter what.

688
00:54:15,080 --> 00:54:18,789
Very well. Dr Schlotkin, do your worst.

689
00:54:18,920 --> 00:54:20,876
My pleasure.

690
00:54:23,760 --> 00:54:25,716
No! Wait! Wait!

691
00:54:26,400 --> 00:54:28,868
I'll tell. I'll tell.

692
00:54:29,280 --> 00:54:31,316
I knew it would work.

693
00:54:31,440 --> 00:54:33,590
All right. Give it to me.

694
00:54:34,680 --> 00:54:36,636
The combination is

695
00:54:38,160 --> 00:54:38,910
one.

696
00:54:39,040 --> 00:54:40,314
- One.
- One.

697
00:54:40,440 --> 00:54:41,236
Two.

698
00:54:41,360 --> 00:54:42,429
- Two.
- Two.

699
00:54:42,560 --> 00:54:43,231
Three.

700
00:54:43,360 --> 00:54:44,429
- Three.
- Three.

701
00:54:44,560 --> 00:54:45,231
Four.

702
00:54:45,360 --> 00:54:46,588
- Four.
- Four.

703
00:54:47,720 --> 00:54:48,470
Five.

704
00:54:48,600 --> 00:54:49,999
- Five.
- Five.

705
00:54:50,560 --> 00:54:55,236
So the combination is
one, two, three, four, five.

706
00:54:55,840 --> 00:54:58,559
That's the stupidest combination
I ever heard!

707
00:54:58,680 --> 00:55:00,830
It's what an idiot has on his luggage.

708
00:55:00,960 --> 00:55:02,757
Thank you, Your Highness.

709
00:55:03,120 --> 00:55:05,554
- What did you do?
- I turned off the wall.

710
00:55:05,680 --> 00:55:07,989
- No, you turned off the movie.
- Wrong button.

711
00:55:08,120 --> 00:55:10,395
- Well, put it back up!
- Yes, sir!

712
00:55:11,000 --> 00:55:14,709
You gotta get that thing fixed! We're back,
and we have the combination.

713
00:55:14,840 --> 00:55:16,796
- Schlotkin!
- What?

714
00:55:16,920 --> 00:55:20,117
We're done. Go back to the golf course
and work on your putts.

715
00:55:20,560 --> 00:55:25,236
Let's go, Arnold. Come, Gretchen.
Of course I'll still have to bill you for this.

716
00:55:28,480 --> 00:55:31,233
Oh! I bet she gives great helmet.

717
00:55:34,040 --> 00:55:37,112
- Did it work?
- Yes, sir. We have the combination.

718
00:55:37,240 --> 00:55:41,870
Great! Now we can take every last breath
of fresh air from Planet Druidia.

719
00:55:42,000 --> 00:55:44,958
- What's the combination?
- One, two, three, four, five.

720
00:55:45,080 --> 00:55:47,036
- One, two, three, four, five?
- Yes.

721
00:55:47,160 --> 00:55:50,755
That's amazing. I've got
the same combination on my luggage.

722
00:55:50,880 --> 00:55:54,509
- Prepare Spaceball One for departure.
- Yes, sir.

723
00:55:54,640 --> 00:55:57,200
And change the combination
on my luggage.

724
00:56:03,720 --> 00:56:06,518
There it is. Spaceball City straight ahead.

725
00:56:06,640 --> 00:56:08,596
Good. I'm taking her in.

726
00:56:11,440 --> 00:56:13,590
What the hell is that thing?

727
00:56:14,000 --> 00:56:16,833
Looks like a Winnebago with wings. Jeez.

728
00:56:16,960 --> 00:56:19,394
Hey, you can't park here!

729
00:56:19,520 --> 00:56:22,398
Yeah. Can't you guys read? "No Parking".

730
00:56:26,840 --> 00:56:28,796
That son of a...

731
00:56:31,680 --> 00:56:35,878
All right, hands up.
You're under arrest for illegal parking.

732
00:56:36,000 --> 00:56:37,752
Yeah!

733
00:56:59,120 --> 00:57:03,511
Warden Miller, Warden Miller
You're wanted in V17

734
00:57:03,640 --> 00:57:08,191
Attention, attention
Section C scanners, report

735
00:57:08,960 --> 00:57:10,313
